<title>UK: Danka shares gain after ADR strength.</title>
<headline>Danka shares gain after ADR strength.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in office equipment supplier Danka Business Systems Plc jumped on Tuesday after a sharp rise in its ADR listing on NASDAQ in New York, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares in London gained 18-1/2p to 515p by 0814 GMT in volume of 61,000 shares.</p>
<p>Danka's ADRS climbed $2-3/8 to $35-1/2, dragged higher by sharp gains on the NASDAQ which closed up 33.91 points, or 2.6 per cent, to 1,339.24.</p>
<p>Dealers said the gains on NASDAQ were fuelled by demand for second-tier stocks.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
